WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.710
A download endpoint should accept an
authorized object ID,

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.448
load tenant-scoped storage metadata,
select the configured root,

3
00:00:07.528 --> 00:00:08.748
and derive the target.

4
00:00:08.828 --> 00:00:12.166
It verifies lexical containment and, when
links are in scope,

5
00:00:12.246 --> 00:00:14.557
real-target containment before opening.

6
00:00:14.637 --> 00:00:19.194
The response uses approved display
metadata rather than exposing the storage path.

7
00:00:19.274 --> 00:00:23.896
Every alternate download or preview route
must apply the same object authorization;

8
00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:27.057
a path inside the root may still belong to
another tenant.

9
00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:31.181
For uploads, generate the temporary and
final storage names on the server.

10
00:00:31.261 --> 00:00:34.535
Preserve the original filename only as
untrusted metadata,

11
00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:38.210
and validate file type, size, and content
under the upload policy.

12
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.563
Keep staging separate from served or
executable locations.

13
00:00:41.643 --> 00:00:46.394
Static assets, templates, and generated
reports should use logical resource mappings

14
00:00:46.474 --> 00:00:50.967
or closed categories instead of combining
request text with directory structure.

15
00:00:51.047 --> 00:00:54.321
These designs reduce how much path syntax
must be validated.

16
00:00:54.401 --> 00:00:58.060
Archive extraction creates many output
paths from entry metadata.

17
00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.836
For every entry, reject unsupported entry
types,

18
00:01:00.916 --> 00:01:04.446
derive the destination beneath one
controlled extraction root,

19
00:01:04.526 --> 00:01:06.709
and verify containment before writing.

20
00:01:06.789 --> 00:01:10.319
Account for link entries, preexisting
links in the destination,

21
00:01:10.399 --> 00:01:13.416
entry count, expanded size, and
replacement behavior.

22
00:01:13.496 --> 00:01:17.797
Use a library mode that exposes enough
entry information to enforce the policy.

23
00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:22.113
Do not assume that validating the
archive's outer filename controls the paths

24
00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:23.285
embedded inside it.

25
00:01:23.365 --> 00:01:27.280
Code review should inventory readFile,
writeFile, unlink, rm, rename,

26
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:32.046
copyFile, streams, file-serving helpers,
upload handlers, and archive extractors.

27
00:01:32.126 --> 00:01:34.309
Trace each path component to its source.

28
00:01:34.389 --> 00:01:37.534
Identify the authorized root, decoding
representation,

29
00:01:37.614 --> 00:01:40.888
lexical containment check, real-filesystem
assumptions,

30
00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:44.627
user and tenant authorization, and
service-account permissions.

31
00:01:44.707 --> 00:01:48.943
Examine whether another route reaches the
object through a weaker mapping and

32
00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:51.848
whether concurrent actors can change
directories.

33
00:01:51.928 --> 00:01:55.522
Tests should cover root equality, siblings
with shared prefixes,

34
00:01:55.602 --> 00:01:59.903
parent escapes, absolute inputs,
unsupported separators for the deployment,

35
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:03.835
links, invalid identifiers, cross-tenant
objects, writes, deletes,

36
00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:07.060
and archive entries without becoming an
exploit catalog.
